---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../../components/Navigation.astro';
---

<Layout title="Shane Lorien - Home">
  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto p-12 bg-white font-sans text-slate-900 leading-relaxed dark:bg-slate-950 dark:text-slate-100 transition-colors duration-300">
    <Navigation />

    <header class="flex justify-between items-start mb-20">
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h1 class="text-6xl font-extrabold tracking-tighter text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Shane Lorien</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-slate-500 font-medium dark:text-slate-400">As by cutting and filing, as by carving and polishing</p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex-shrink-0">
        <img src="/MyPage/avatar.jpg" alt="Avatar" class="w-28 h-28 rounded-full border border-slate-100 shadow-sm object-cover dark:border-slate-800" />
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-24">
      <!-- About Section -->
      <section class="grid grid-cols-[140px,1fr] gap-8 items-start">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest text-slate-400 uppercase mt-1">About</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          <p>
            Hello, I’m Guan Yu Chen, a 2025 undergraduate student in Computer Science at Peking University, School of Information Science and Technology.
          </p>
          <p>
            My interests are still developing, and I’m currently exploring different directions. I have preliminary interest in LLM, NLP, CV, and I’m also self-studying related content such as CS241N.
            In spring 2026, I applied for the Peking University Innovation + Workstation project “Dog Intent Recognition via Pose and Voiceprint,” and passed the proposal defense; I’m now advancing the project. I also participate in AI Infra Seminars organized by LCPU and the Peking University supercomputing team, and I have a preliminary understanding of AI infrastructure.
            Besides my academic interests, I also enjoy piano, writing, and Daoyin. You can find some of my reflections and notes on my lifestyle blog:
            <a href="https://logic61.github.io/" class="text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">https://logic61.github.io/</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Education Section -->
      <section class="grid grid-cols-[140px,1fr] gap-8 items-start">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest text-slate-400 uppercase mt-1">Education</h2>
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1">
            <h3 class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">Peking University</h3>
            <span class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">2025 - Present</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-slate-600 mb-2 dark:text-slate-300">School of Information Science and Technology</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Computer Science Undergraduate</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 mt-2 dark:text-slate-500">Relevant coursework: Programming Practice, Fundamentals of AI, etc.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Skills Section -->
      <section class="grid grid-cols-[140px,1fr] gap-8 items-start">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest text-slate-400 uppercase mt-1">Skills</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-y-6 gap-x-4 text-sm">
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-medium text-slate-900 mb-2">Programming Languages</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-slate-50 rounded text-slate-600">C++</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-slate-50 rounded text-slate-600">Python</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-slate-50 rounded text-slate-600">PyTorch</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-slate-50 rounded text-slate-600">CUDA / Triton / TileLang (beginner)</span>
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="col-span-2">
            <h3 class="font-medium text-slate-900 mb-2">Tools & Others</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-600 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
              <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-slate-50 rounded text-slate-600">Git / GitHub</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-slate-50 rounded text-slate-600">LaTeX</span>
              <span class="px-2 py-1 bg-slate-50 rounded text-slate-600">Markdown</span>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Projects Section -->
      <section class="grid grid-cols-[140px,1fr] gap-8 items-start">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest text-slate-400 uppercase mt-1">Selected Projects</h2>
        <div class="space-y-10">
          <div class="group">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
              <h3 class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 group-hover:text-blue-600 dark:group-hover:text-blue-400 transition-colors">
                <a href="https://github.com/Logic61/PKU-Planner" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PKU-Planner</a>
              </h3>
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/50 px-2 py-1 rounded">C++</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm mb-3">A course and deadline assistant adapted to the Peking University teaching website</p>
            <ul class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside">
              <li>Visually driven task reminders; tasks change color according to urgency</li>
              <li>Supports importing courses from the teaching website and through screenshots</li>
              <li>Enables one-click AI-generated personalized suggestions based on course and deadline information</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="group">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
              <h3 class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 group-hover:text-blue-600 dark:group-hover:text-blue-400 transition-colors">
                <a href="https://github.com/Logic61/Obsidian-to-Hexo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Obsidian-to-Hexo</a>
              </h3>
              <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900/50 px-2 py-1 rounded">Python</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 text-sm mb-3">An automation tool for migrating Obsidian Markdown notes to a Hexo blog</p>
            <ul class="text-sm text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside">
              <li>Parses and converts Obsidian-specific Markdown syntax</li>
              <li>Automatically adapts and transfers files into Hexo’s posts directory and organizes metadata</li>
              <li>Written in Python to enable batch backup and publishing workflows</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Hobbies & Skills Section -->
      <section class="grid grid-cols-[140px,1fr] gap-8 items-start">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest text-slate-400 dark:text-slate-500 uppercase mt-1">Hobbies & Skills</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div class="group">
            <h3 class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Piano</h3>
            <ul class="text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-1.5 list-none">
              I’ve played some well-known Chopin pieces such as the first ballade, the Grande Polonaise, and pieces like “Liebestraum” and “The Snow”.
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="group">
            <h3 class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Daoyin</h3>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-sm text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
              I joined the Peking University Daoyin team and won fourth place in the group event for Wu Qin Xi at the 2026 Spring Capital Universities Fitness Qigong competition.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

  </main>
</Layout>